    "summary": "Yemen's internationally recognized government has warned that Houthi forces are attempting to take control of the Bab al-Mandeb strait, mirroring Iran's strategy in the Strait of Hormuz. The move threatens global shipping through a key Red Sea chokepoint.",
    "content": "Yemen's legitimate government, recognized by the international community, has raised alarm over Houthi efforts to dominate the Bab al-Mandeb strait, a critical maritime passage linking the Red Sea, the Gulf of Aden, and the Indian Ocean. Foreign Minister Afrah al-Zouba, speaking to media at the Yemeni embassy in Riyadh, stated that the Houthis aim to replicate Iran's approach in the Strait of Hormuz by controlling the movement of international vessels through this strategic waterway.\n\nThis development follows years of conflict in Yemen, where the Houthi group has steadily expanded its military capabilities, including drone and missile strikes targeting Saudi Arabia and UAE interests. The group has previously attacked commercial ships in the Red Sea, but this explicit ambition to control Bab al-Mandeb represents a significant escalation. The strait sees about 10% of global maritime trade, including oil and natural gas shipments from the Gulf to Europe and North America.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this situation carries direct implications. Many Somalis rely on shipping routes that pass through the Bab al-Mandeb for trade and humanitarian aid. Any disruption could raise costs for essential goods and remittances sent to family members in Somalia. Additionally, instability at this chokepoint may affect the safety of dhows and small vessels used by Somali traders and fishermen.\n\nAl-Zouba urged the international community to take preventive action, warning that failure to address the Houthi threat could lead to a crisis comparable to the tensions in the Strait of Hormuz. He emphasized that maritime security in the region is vital not only for Yemen but for global economic stability. The Bab al-Mandeb is also crucial for naval operations against piracy off the Somali coast, a concern for diaspora communities with ties to the maritime sector.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/07/28/xuutiyiinta-oo-isku-dayay-xakameynta-marin-biyoodka-bab-al-mandeb-si-lamid-ah-sida-iiraan-uga-taliso-hormuz/",
